        "title": "Understanding Cross-Entropy Loss",
        "text": "Cross-entropy loss measures the difference between the true labels and the predicted probabilities. It is calculated using the formula: $$-\\sum y \\ln\\left(p\\right)+\\left(1-y\\right) \\ln\\left(1-p\\right)$$, where $$y$$ is the true label and $$p$$ is the predicted probability.",
